customer: activist_guy
problem: bad_ram
brief:
	Really a hacker; the player's character calls him the activist. He knows what is wrong, asks for new RAM and says little. His computer holds hints that he researches Cambion.

== drop-off
(neutral) Hello! Have you got a minute?
- Busy day?
	(neutral) Always. The newsletter doesn't write itself.
- Nice button. What's it for?
	(happy) Saving the old park from the parking lot people. Sign our petition sometime!

- So, what's your problem?
	(problem) My computer counts up its memory, and then it just stops. It never gets to Windows.
	- Did anything change lately?
	- That's unfortunate. Can you remember doing anything special before it started to act up?
	(neutral) My nephew put more memory in it last month.
	(angry) It was meant to be faster!
	- OK, leave it with me. Have a Funtastic day!
		(neutral) I need it for the newsletter, so please be quick.
		- I'll do my best. Have a Funtastic day!

== pick-up
(neutral) It starts again? Wonderful.
- Happy I could help.
	(neutral) Was it the new memory?
	- Yeah.
- That upgrade...
(irritated02) Yeah, I figured. I'll have a word with my nephew.
- Maybe come back here next time you need an upgrade and I'll throw in a discount for you.
	(happy) Thanks dude. I'll keep that in mind.
	- Take care now.
